=== 2026-09-05, re-scored on a fourth review of pull request 84 ===
Re-run of score.py against the same committed output/shares.json and
output/states_meta.json. No state was rebuilt and no decomposition was run: this
stage reads the committed share tables only. Three changes to the scoring script,
all of them additions. First, the script now refuses to produce final verdicts,
tables or a figure unless the shares file covers layers 0 to 11 for every arm the
scoring reads and does not mark itself partial_run: true. Until now the script
took its layer list from whichever layers the file happened to hold, so a
decomposition run over the six band layers alone would have supplied every layer a
verdict needs and the outputs would have looked final. The option --allow-partial
permits a diagnostic scoring instead, which writes every file under a .partial.
name, stamps both JSON files, labels the figure and the comma-separated table, and
rewrites each verdict string to say it is not a verdict. The committed shares file
passes as complete: all twelve layers for every family in all seven arms the
scoring reads, which is the lens and the six controls. Second, the
iteration-safety-bound check now counts the decompositions that carry the flag and
the decompositions that do not, and refuses a file holding both, because a partial
decomposition merged into the committed pre-flag file would otherwise be reported
as clear everywhere while the untouched entries were scored with their termination
status unknown. The committed file holds 672 arm-family-layer groups and none of
them carries the field, so the check reports that it cannot be applied, which is
the second line of the run below. Third, the comparison specification section 7.1
asks to be reported beside H6 and expressly keeps out of its rule, the same
five-against-eighteen Mann-Whitney test carried out on the norm-matched
random-dictionary control shares, is now run at every layer, pooled over the three
control seeds and once per seed; the first version of the script recorded the two
control medians and never ran the test. Effect on the record: every value that
existed in the previous verdicts.json is unchanged, a key-by-key comparison of the
old and new files found 207 leaf values added, 0 changed and 0 removed, and
per_layer_tables.json, per_layer_shares.csv and exp011_share_curves.png are
byte-identical to their committed versions. All four verdicts reproduce: H6 NOT
SUPPORTED, H16 NOT SUPPORTED, H16a NOT SUPPORTED, H16b SUPPORTED. The added
control comparison separates nothing at any band layer, with one-sided p between
0.1298 and 0.8792 in the basins-greater direction and between 0.1237 and 0.8733 in
the reverse direction, against a 0.05 threshold. Running the script twice in
succession gave a byte-identical verdicts.json. The readout stage was not re-run:
its gate change is a refusal path, and its committed outputs predate the metadata
block it now writes.
